    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 654 of 1927",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A6527\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 654 of the laws of 1927,\nrelation to joint water works systems, in relation to compensation paid\nto members of the board of trustees of the Westchester joint water works\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: Section 1 amends Subdivision 7 of\nSection 3 of chapter 654 of the laws of 1972, raising the limit of trus-\ntee compensation from $100 to $300 per meeting.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: The members of the Board of Trustees had not had an\nincrease in compensation for over 15 years, prior to 2006; a slight\nincrease was authorized from the prior per meeting amount ($60), but the\ncomplexity of running the utility has added a significant number of\nhours to their management responsibilities. They have requested the\nauthority to consider an increase for an amount not to exceed $300 per\nmeeting. Any actual increase will be the decision of the Board of Trus-\ntees, all of whom are the chief elected officials of the jurisdictions\nserved by the Joint Water Works: the Town of Mamaroneck, the Village of\nMamaroneck, and the Town/Village of Harrison.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  2005-06: A.10388-B (Latimer) Signed Chapter\n232 2005-06: S.7444-B (Oppenheimer) Signed Chapter 232\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the State\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
