    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Westchester County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A6527A               REVISED 07/21/09\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend chapter 654 of the laws of 1927, relating to joint water\nworks systems, in relation to compensation paid to members of the board\nof trustees of the Westchester joint water works\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo allow the Westchester Joint Water Works, a non-profit utility, the\nauthority to increase the per meeting compensation of the members of the\nBoard of Trustees.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 amends Subdivision 7 of Section 3 of chapter 654 of the laws\nof 1972, raising the limit of trustee compensation from $100 to $300 per\nmeeting.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe members of the Board of Trustees had not had an increase in compen-\nsation for over 15 years, prior to 2006; a slight increase was author-\nized from the prior per meeting amount ($60), but the complexity of\nrunning the utility has added a significant number of hours to their\nmanagement responsibilities. They have requested the authority to\nconsider an increase for an amount not to exceed $300 per meeting. Any\nactual increase will be the decision of the Board of Trustees, all of\nwhom are the chief elected officials of the jurisdictions served by the\nJoint Water Works: the Town of Mamaroneck, the Village of Mamaroneck,\nand the Town/Village of Harrison.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2005-06: A.10388-B (Latimer) Signed Chapter 232 2005-06: S.7444-B\n(Oppenheimer) Signed Chapter 232\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
